{
  "$comment": "The keyboard contract: one table of keys per WAI-ARIA pattern. A component joins a pattern through `pattern` in registry.json, or one of its parts does through `partPatterns`, and src/stories/KeyboardContract.stories.tsx presses every row here against every component that names the pattern, in both reading directions, so each row is a tested fact. The component pages, the per-component markdown and the published schemas print these rows; scripts/validate-keyboard-patterns.mjs holds the three together. A row's `id` is the check the story runs, `keys` are KeyboardEvent.key names (the space bar written Space), a row no key starts has empty `keys` and a `when` that says what does, and `inline: true` marks a pair that swaps in a right-to-left layout.",
